Puerts JsEnv on V8 9.4 (the Mac build, puerts-ue58-mac.patch): turn on WebAssembly reference types (externref) for
the page's V8 before it starts. wasm-bindgen and newer Rust toolchains emit them by default, and V8 9.4 rejects such
modules unless the flag is set (shipped from V8 9.6). The bridge's own worker isolates use a separate static copy of V8
and set the same flag themselves (Source/JsGameBridge/Private/JsgbWasmFeatures.cpp).
Apply from inside the Puerts folder, after puerts-ue58-mac.patch: git apply --ignore-whitespace <this file>

--- a/Source/JsEnv/Private/JsEnvModule.cpp
+++ b/Source/JsEnv/Private/JsEnvModule.cpp
@@ -215,6 +215,12 @@
 
 #if defined(WITH_V8_BYTECODE)
     v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString("--no-lazy --no-flush-bytecode --no-enable-lazy-source-positions");
+#endif
+
+#if V8_MAJOR_VERSION < 10
+    // WebAssembly reference types (externref), which wasm-bindgen and newer Rust toolchains emit by default: shipped in
+    // V8 9.6, complete behind this flag in 9.4. Without it such modules fail to compile (Spark's splat worker).
+    v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString("--experimental-wasm-reftypes");
 #endif
 
     // v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString("--expose-gc");
